The Cambodian Constitution states that all mineral resources are the property of the State, and that the management of such resources shall be set out by law.11 To date there is no law covering oil and gas in Cambodia, and the sector is currently governed by the amended Petroleum Regulations from 1991. Under the Petroleum Regulations of 1991, the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy (MIME) was the administrative authority responsible for the management of petroleum resources.
