An economic land concession (ELC) is a long-term lease that allows a concessionaire to clear land in order to develop industrial-scale agriculture, and can be granted for various activities including large-scale plantations, raising animals, and building factories to process agricultural products.1
As stated in theNational Strategic Development Plan (NSDP) for 2014-2018, the Cambodian government’s vision is to modernize Cambodia’s agriculture and transform the sector to utilize new technologies and techniques, as well as to diversify agricultural activities in an environmentally sustainable way.5 The overall objectives of ELCs are to:
to generate state revenues through economic land use fees, taxation and related services charges.6
