Economic land concessions Formalized in the 2001 Land Law, an economic land concession (ELC) is a long-term lease that allows a concessionaire to clear land in order to develop industrial-scale agriculture.
It is difficult to assess exactly how many ELCs have been approved, which concessions are active, and how much state revenue has been raised in the process. According to MAFF data, between 1996 and June 2012, MAFF signed ELC contracts with 118 companies covering a total land area of 1,204,750 hectares.36However, some NGO reports have claimed the figure is closer to 2 million hectares.37
