Development of water infrastructure, water policy and administration are essential for Cambodia, particularly for guaranteeing clean water for drinking and sanitation, and water for irrigation purposes.
The policies enacted in recent decades show that water management is usually a part of wider policies regarding economic development, natural disaster, improved sanitation and more recently, climate change. The two most important plans in the governmental hierarchy are the Rectangular Strategy phase III and the National Strategic Development Plan with a budget of 26.59 billion USD4.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forests and Fisheries responsible for implements policies with implications for irrigation and catchments, both in forests and fisheries areas.
