Fernando Botero Angulo is a figurative artist and sculptor in Colombia. Born in Medellin, his iconic style, also known as the “zombie”, depicts people who are fat and big, have a fleshy texture, and have a sense of criticism and humor.
Botello’s monumental public sculptures could be seen on the streets of New York and Paris. His depiction of the obesity of the character has become his iconic style and is immediately considered to be the creation of Botero around the world.
