Gloves have been used in football for decades for a variety of reasons.
Football gloves give you an extra edge on the pitch by improving your grip on the ball. Good gloves give players an edge over their opponents.
Football is an aggressive sport. In every position on the field (except the kicker) the hands are used in some way and protection is therefore a necessary aspect of preparation.
Wearing gloves gives you confidence on the pitch.
That's why football gloves have evolved over time to not only protect against the cold, but also reduce the number of injuries.
Furthermore, they were not intended to make handling the ball easier. Therefore, only the players who had little contact with the ball wore gloves, such as the linemen.
Gloves have evolved enormously over time. Not only have they acquired additional functions such as improving grip, but they have also become a stylish accessory.
Today, the gloves look like true works of art and players buy them in all colors and designs.
The main functions of gloves are to protect your hands from injuries and the cold and to improve your performance.
The price varies according to the quality of the brand and the type of glove. Below is a price overview to help you manage your budget.
Gloves are expensive between 60-100 dollars. These are high prices, but at least you can be sure that you have high-quality gloves that will last for seasons.
Most gloves fall into this category and are around $30 and $60. These are also of high quality, are durable and will last at least a season.
Cheap gloves are between 15 and 35 dollars. However, with these models you cannot assume that you will receive gloves of good quality.
Why do football gloves lose their grip over time?
Gripping a football, the weather conditions and trying to “restore the grip” (ie wetting the gloves and rubbing them together) will all cause your gloves to lose their grip over time.
While it may seem like an unfair advantage, Grip Boost is currently legal on all levels of play.
Although gloves sometimes seem to last 2-3 seasons, it is recommended to buy a new pair for every season.
However, a receiver or running back should purchase 2-3 pairs of gloves for each season, as their gloves should have maximum tack all season long.
It is important to read the care instructions that come with your gloves.
Skill players' gloves must maintain their adhesive strength or they will lose their target.
And if you are going to wash them in the washing machine, always choose a delicate program with cold water. Then hang them to air dry.
There are two methods of finding your size, it is best to use both as some brands may vary in measurement methods.
The gloves should enclose your hands well, but should not impede blood flow.
Lineman gloves have a limited grip. The palms are made of leather, and designed to withstand rough handling and to protect the hands while blocking and tackling.
Hopefully, with this article I've provided you with all the information you need to help you find the best gloves to secure your performance on the pitch.
Linemen need reinforced gloves for protection. And players who defend and handle the ball need a hybrid glove.
Decisions about colors and patterns are made based on personal preference. Money spent on good quality gloves really is worth every penny!
