For example, the Voltric 0 is available in two versions: the 3U and the 4U. But you could make it harder by following the tips in the balance point section above.
The disadvantage of heavy rackets is that it is much more difficult to control. You fundamentally sacrifice control in favor of strength, and unless you are highly skilled, this could be a problem.
It is important to choose the right shape of the frame. The current models offer you two options: the traditional oval shape and the isometric frames.
Oval shape: This conventional shape has a trickier sweet spot, but if you manage to land the shuttle on it, you'll get an excellent quality shot. Therefore, to get the most out of the oval shape, you need to be highly skilled so that you can achieve a high success rate by landing the shuttle in the desired spot on the racket.
The stem: flexible or stiff?
The stiff stem: It has less bounce, which is compensated with more powerful swing.
The repulsion is notably better than a stiff stem, this allows you to deliver pretty good speed without too much effort.
They are also slower than stiff-handled rackets. This can be a problem for many people as it reduces the speed of your returns and attacks.
Ultimately, it is a good choice for defensive style players. Because you don't have to whip very hard, you can focus more on defensive shots and your strategy in general.
