A facemask is part of your American football helmet and protects your face, especially the sensitive parts such as the mouth, nose and eyes.
Many (beginning) football athletes tend to choose a facemask with as many bars as possible - because that would offer the most protection - but it is not that easy.
Since a facemask has a safety function, I certainly do not recommend buying this item on a whim.
It is essential for your own safety - and of course for your wallet - that you buy the right facemask for your helmet.
Are you curious about other good options?
2 Extensive American Football facemask review
Please read the following information carefully so that you can make an informed choice.
There are three types of materials used for facemasks, namely carbon steel, stainless steel and titanium.
Being lighter, they can give experienced players an edge and improve their speed.
Titanium gives players a remarkable advantage on the pitch, keeping them faster, more agile and better conditioned for long matches.
Another possible goal is to improve vision. Some facemasks can function like sunglasses to improve your vision when your eyes come into contact with extremely bright light.
Based on your position in the field, some facemasks are more suitable than others. The bar configuration of a facemask determines your performance and the degree of protection.
This won't help a quarterback or wide receiver much, for example, as they need a full view to perform their duties on the field.
Offensive linemen – along with defensive linemen are the players who experience the most physical contact – would be in big trouble if they wore them, and got the hands of the opponents in their faces.
In general, you can choose from two types of facemasks: an open and a more closed facemask.
These types of facemasks often have many horizontal bars that run across the bottom half of the mask.
For some positions, sight is the key to success. For them, an open cage around the eyes is essential to ensure maximum visibility.
There are a number of open cage models that provide additional protection for 'skill players' (the positions that usually handle the ball and are most responsible for scoring points).
The right facemask must be able to balance protection and performance.
What distinguishes the best football facemasks from the 'standard' facemasks are their 'special features'.
These advanced features will offer a player that little bit of extra protection. In addition, they will allow a better view and therefore a better performance.
In addition, they will also be more effective in protecting your mouth and teeth, in preventing injuries and concussions.
So often only a Xenith facemask fits on a Xenith helmet, and the same applies to the other brands.
Meets the needs of different players and positions
The Schutt DNA Ropo is the perfect choice if you have to or want to watch your money, but still want to buy a good facemask. Robustness and durability are not compromised.
In addition, it is one of the most durable facemasks for football, made of carbon steel. The facemask is specially designed for large Schutt DNA helmets, but also fits on the DNA Pro+ (Elite) helmets.
ROPO therefore stands for Reinforced Oral Protection Only.
This facemask is made of stainless steel – which makes it lightweight – and is appreciated by many athletes. Especially experienced players like to choose this product.
The protection is provided in such a way that it will not restrict your view. On the contrary; it will even improve your vision!
The facemask is 20% lighter than other helmets thanks to the quality stainless steel construction with thinner bars.
The facemask is very solid and built to last. Keep in mind that the facemask is a bit on the expensive side and you don't get a hardware kit with it.
Then this is probably the best facemask you can choose.
Best American Football Facemask for All Positions & Carbon Steel: Xenith Prime
The only drawback of this product is – again – that it only fits helmets from Xenith itself. But be careful!
It is also nice that the manufacturer has paid a lot of attention to adding specific instructions regarding installation. Installation is simple and you can do it at home without any problems.
The Xenith Prime facemask is recommended for football players looking for an open facemask for a better view of the field.
Another great aspect of this facemask is that it comes in different colors. Whichever you choose, you will always look cool.
Great freedom of movement and reduction of areas of potential impact
Please note that this facemask is primarily intended for certain positions (running backs, wide receivers, defensive ends and tight ends).
Then rather look for another model facemask from Schutt.
This product has a high price tag, but that is fully justified given the premium features.
Schutt has added mouth protection to this facemask by means of sturdy bars. Players can move completely freely without fear of a sudden impact.
This material is very durable while keeping weight to a minimum. Moving smoothly on the pitch will no longer be a dream.
You can also choose from 13 different colors. You will feel confident and stand out with this product.
Always check whether the facemask you have in mind is actually compatible with your helmet!
), you can choose the right facemask.
Which facemasks are used for the different positions?
If you're willing to pay a little for your facemask to ensure the highest level of protection, you can go for titanium, which is the strongest and lightest of the three, but also the most pricey.
If you want to stick to a budget, carbon steel is ideal. It is the most affordable, while still meeting the standard of the football industry.
It is not always easy to find a suitable facemask. You should do some research and evaluate the products carefully before making a decision.
