Such a shoulder pad may look a bit complicated. It therefore consists of several parts.
The first part to look out for is the neck. It is the V-shaped or circular opening that you can slide your head through.
This part is usually made of strong and durable material, so that all parts of the shoulder pads stay in place, regardless of your playing style or field position.
The flap is an extended part of the shoulder pads, which is added at the very top. It offers extra protection to the shoulder joint, shoulder blade and other parts.
The cup is smaller than the flap, but has the same shape and sits under the outer flap.
The attachment, sometimes referred to as a 'bias', is an additional inner cushion that can absorb the shock of a sudden impact with other players.
